# The code generator's surface: what nupp.compiler.aot.llvm.codegen calls in
# the pinned LLVM and lld, linked statically either into the code generator
# library (scripts/toolchain codegen-library) or into a Nupp host built with
# `native-codegen`.
#
# Each line is `ALIAS TARGET`, optionally followed by `darwin` or `!darwin` for
# a target spelled differently on one standard library. The linker exports the
# target under the alias and keeps every LLVM, lld and C++ name local, so a
# process that loads another LLVM (Mesa's llvmpipe Vulkan driver does) never
# has its calls bound to this one. The compiler declares each alias with an
# `asm` label, so a change here is a change to codegen.nupp's declarations too
# (tests/tools/toolchain/toolchaintest.lua holds the two together).
#
# The LLVM C API covers parsing, verifying, optimizing and emitting. What it
# lacks is reached by its Itanium-mangled C++ name: lld's drivers, a file stream
# for their messages, crash recovery around a link, and the archive writer.

